From 766d073553f64e5504506412c064d76de9303bbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:40:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] samfdeepcnv: keep sub-cloud layers within the cloud-base CFL
 limit

xmbmax bounds the cloud-base mass flux by the CFL limit of layer kbcon,
where eta = 1. Below cloud base eta(k) = eta(k+1) / (1 + (xlamue - xlamud) dz),
and xlamud = 0.001 clamt exceeds xlamue = clamt / z above about 1 km, so for
elevated convection eta grows downward; with the TKE-scaled clamt at its cap
it about doubles per layer. Those layers then exceed CFL 1 and the explicit
compensating subsidence overshoots.

Also bound xmbmax by dp / (g dt eta) over kb <= k < kbcon.

Measured, hafs_global_1nest_atm: develop has 257 single-step SAMF heatings
> 4 K, 253 with layer CFL > 1, the largest 24.5 K at CFL 24; with this
change none exceeds 4 K, and mean precipitation changes by -0.19 % (two
consv_te-perturbed members differ by 0.02 %). With other pending physics
fixes the same test crashed at 5.5 h (+70.7 K in one step at CFL 54, eta 51,
compute_qs table overflow); with this change it completes, largest CFL 0.85.

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/CONV/SAMF/samfdeepcnv.f | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/physics/CONV/SAMF/samfdeepcnv.f b/physics/CONV/SAMF/samfdeepcnv.f
index 8f862c9b..3e7aabc0 100644
--- a/physics/CONV/SAMF/samfdeepcnv.f
+++ b/physics/CONV/SAMF/samfdeepcnv.f
@@ -1612,6 +1612,16 @@ c
      &              * dt2)
         endif
       enddo
+!  sub-cloud eta can exceed 1 (detrainment > entrainment above ~1 km): keep CFL <= 1 there too
+      do k = 1, km
+        do i = 1, im
+          if(cnvflg(i) .and. k >= kb(i) .and. k < kbcon(i)) then
+            dp = 1000.0_conv_wp * del(i,k)
+            xmbmax(i) = min(xmbmax(i), dp /
+     &        (real(grav, kind=conv_wp) * dt2 * eta(i,k)))
+          endif
+        enddo
+      enddo
 c
 c  compute cloud moisture property and precipitation
 c
